md(r"""
**Decisions 5–8**
- **Target encoded as 1/0:** models need numeric targets. Churn = 1 is the "positive" class, because it is the event we want to detect.
- **Merged "No internet service"/"No phone service" into "No":** these categories say the same thing as the column that controls them (`InternetService`, `PhoneService`), so keeping them would create redundant, highly correlated features.
- **One-hot encoding:** logistic regression can't use text like "Month-to-month". One-hot encoding turns each category into a 0/1 column. Ordinary numbers (1, 2, 3) would wrongly imply an order between categories. `drop_first=True` removes one redundant column per variable to avoid perfect collinearity.
- **Scaling** is done after the train/test split (Part 5) so that no information from the test set leaks into training.
""")

